WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.520
A drawing room.

2
00:00:01.570 --> 00:00:03.080
A shaded lamp.

3
00:00:03.130 --> 00:00:06.100
On the table, a heavy iron box.

4
00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:08.110
A poker levers the clasp.

5
00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:09.640
The lid swings up.

6
00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:11.390
A fortune is gone.

7
00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.930
And Watson cries, "Thank God!"

8
00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.470
A fortune lost, and he's glad.

9
00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:19.070
Why would anyone celebrate that?

10
00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:22.300
In this mission, you'll
meet Watson as the narrator:

11
00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:27.310
an army doctor, wounded in Afghanistan,
telling the story long afterwards.

12
00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:32.600
You'll meet Mary Morstan, a governess
whose father vanished in 1878.

13
00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:35.890
And you'll read the two scenes
on either side of the box,

14
00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:37.960
in Watson's own words.

15
00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:42.260
Your mission: explain why
Watson is glad the box is empty.
